# guv-gitignore — marker: the /guv:scaffold deploy appends its block only when this line is absent

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# guv core — the entries every guv-governed project needs.
# /guv:scaffold appends exactly this block (markers included) to a
# pre-existing .gitignore; keep it self-contained and stack-agnostic.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# guv-core-start
# Environment & secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
secrets/
*.pem
*.key
*-service-account.json
*-credentials.json
# Claude Code: personal overrides, not committed
.claude/settings.local.json
# Auto-generated agent memory — the evaluator / reviewer write this
# on the first /eval or /handoff (/guv:-namespaced under the plugin).
# Ignored by default so it doesn't sit untracked in every consumer project.
# A team that wants shared agent memory can force-add it
# (git add -f .claude/agent-memory/) and remove this line.
.claude/agent-memory/
# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
# Docker sandbox (opt-in tier)
sandbox/*.log
sandbox/tmp/
# guv lane worktrees (guv-lane.sh — fan-out dispatch)
.worktrees/
# guv lane failure reports + collected lane outputs (lane-dispatch.sh — scratch)
.lane-reports/
# guv continuation checkpoint (continuation-checkpoint.sh PreCompact hook — a
# resume breadcrumb rewritten on every compaction; runtime artifact, not tracked)
.claude/continuation-checkpoint.json
# guv context-wall migration-nudge marker ([16.2]; context-management.sh surface —
# a machine-local did-fire flag so the one-time grandfather nudge fires once, not
# every session; runtime artifact, not tracked)
.claude/.context-wall-migration-nudged
# guv context-wall approach-warning marker ([16.4]; occupancy-meter.sh — a
# machine-local, SESSION-scoped did-fire flag (it stores the session_id) so the
# hard-stop warn-band fires its one-shot approach warning once per session; runtime
# artifact, not tracked)
.claude/.context-wall-approach-warned
# guv context-wall continue-guidance marker ([16.4]; context-management.sh surface —
# a machine-local did-fire flag so the one-shot continue-mode "author a window if you
# want an explicit compaction point" guidance fires once, not every session; runtime
# artifact, not tracked)
.claude/.context-wall-continue-guided
# guv metering runtime artifact (handoff Step 3 writes the measured suite
# runtime here; meter.sh reads it — transient, rewritten each session, not
# tracked). The committed append-only metering logs (metering.ndjson /
# calibration.ndjson) are deliberately NOT ignored — they are shared evidence.
.claude/metering/.last-suite-runtime
# guv recorded battery verdict (battery-result.sh — run-core-tests.sh records its
# verdict here so the QA stages downstream read it instead of each paying for its
# own battery run). Machine-local and tree-specific: it carries a fingerprint of
# the exact working tree it ran against, so a committed copy would be stale for
# everyone who pulled it.
.claude/metering/.last-battery-result
# guv-core-end

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Dependencies
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules/
.pnp.*
.yarn/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Build output
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.next/
out/
dist/
build/
*.tsbuildinfo

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Testing
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
coverage/
test-results/
playwright-report/
blob-report/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# IDE & editors
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
*.code-workspace

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Logs
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Python
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# Misc
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────
*.bak
*.tmp
*.temp
